      "id": "p8811ev",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is defined as the capacity of a body to perform work.",
        "Kinetic Energy is the energy possessed by an object due to its motion (KE = ½ mv²).",
        "Potential Energy is the energy stored in an object due to its position or configuration (PE = mgh).",
        "The Law of Conservation of Energy states that energy can neither be created nor destroyed, only transformed.",
        "Power represents the rate at which work is done or energy is consumed (P = Work / Time)."
      ],
      "id": "9fpo8or"
    },
